{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/118226","id":3490798809,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7QEVzZ","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118226","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118226.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118226.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118226","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/118226/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/118226/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118226/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/ffdda126fc8a8e01ff549a43566da82696a18c22","number":118226,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Editor: Add resumable download with retry for export templates","user":{"login":"Infiland","id":88491175,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4NDkxMTc1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/88491175?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Infiland","html_url":"https://github.com/Infiland","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Infiland/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Infiland/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Infiland/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Infiland/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Infiland/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Infiland/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Infiland/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Infiland/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Infiland/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Summary\r\n\r\n- Export template downloads now automatically retry (up to 3 times) when the connection drops, resuming from where they left off using HTTP Range headers\r\n- Adds stall detection with a \"Retry Now\" button that appears after 30 seconds of no data, allowing users to manually reconnect without freezing the editor\r\n- Adds `keep_partial_download` and `append_to_download_file` properties to `HTTPRequest` to support partial file preservation and HTTP 206 resume\r\n\r\nFixes #108952\r\nCloses: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/118795\r\n\r\n## Context\r\n\r\nGitHub changed their release downloads to use JWT tokens that expire after ~5 minutes. Export templates are ~1.1 GB, so users on slower connections get cut off mid-download with \"Can't connect to the mirror\" and must restart from zero. This is widely reported across platforms and connection speeds.\r\n\r\n## How it works\r\n\r\n1. When a connection error occurs mid-download, the partial `.tpz` file is preserved and a new request is sent with a `Range: bytes=<offset>-` header\r\n2. If the server responds with `206 Partial Content`, the new data is appended to the existing file\r\n3. If the server responds with `200` (no Range support), the file is overwritten and downloaded fresh\r\n4. If the server responds with `416 Range Not Satisfiable`, the partial file is deleted and the download restarts\r\n5. If the download stalls (no bytes received for 30 seconds), a \"Retry Now\" button appears so the user can abandon the stuck connection and retry immediately\r\n\r\n## Testing notes\r\n\r\nTo test this on a locally compiled build, you will need to temporarily modify `_get_downloads_availability()` in `editor/export/export_template_manager.cpp` to return `DOWNLOADS_AVAILABLE` (since dev builds disable template downloads), and hardcode the mirror version string in `_refresh_mirrors()` to an existing release like `\"4.4.1.stable\"` (since there is no mirror list for unreleased versions).","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"http